 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **KLT Decorrelation:** Applying Karhunen-Loève Transform (KLT) over SH-transformed coefficients ("RAHT+KLT") does not improve performance because SH decomposition already decorrelates the channels sufficiently [S1].
-*   **Method Selection:** RAHT outperforms Predlift due to the low correlation of neighbors' attributes in PlenOctrees [S1].
-*   **Precision:** The scaling step introduces slight quality degradation, which is inherent to the lossy compression [S1].
+*   **KLT Application:** Applying KLT to SH coefficients does not improve performance and should be avoided [S1].
+*   **Precision:** The scaling step introduces quantization error. The choice of $T$ is critical; incorrect $T$ values lead to clipping or poor dynamic range utilization [S1].
+*   **Structure Preservation:** Geometry must be encoded losslessly. Any loss in geometry breaks the PlenOctree structure, making it incompatible with the fast renderer [S1].
